          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; event-level conclusion remains unverified\n\nThe relevant manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for the **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not available in the supplied records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event details |\n\nThe timestamp above is reproduced exactly; the source supplies **no timezone or UTC offset**.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\nThe supplied *Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B* documentation, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225**, states that new transactions created after Pending Close that fall in that period or an earlier period **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Previously entered transactions continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nThus, a newly created, non-exempt manufacturing transaction would be expected to remain held rather than be processed during Pending Close. However, I cannot compare that rule with this event’s recorded status.\n\n### Evidence limitation\nThe available database extract contains work-order and cost-period rows but **no cost-event rows**. Repeated retrieval of the assigned supporting records returned **“Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”** This is a missing-evidence limitation—not evidence that no late event occurred.\n\nThe incomplete audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_bd27b2f6b80e/audit-report.json`. **No database records were changed.**",
